# Loaded via `node --env-file` by the "test" npm script only.
#
# Without this, any test that exercises a real Poller/dispatch failure path
# (logDeviceError, logging/error-log.ts) writes real CSV files under
# packages/backend/data/ — several test files were found doing exactly that
# (devices/routes.test.ts among them) after `data/logs/*.csv` full of test
# fixture IPs turned up in the working tree. Redirecting the whole test run's
# data dir here, instead of patching every test file that might transitively
# hit that code path, is the one-time fix.
PPC_DATA_DIR=.test-data
